   MODIFICATIONS TO THIS WORK (as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(b)):

   The pt-BR data distributed here is a MODIFIED DERIVATIVE of the Shopping
   Queries Dataset. The following changes were made:

     a) Subsetting. Only the US / English locale was retained, and only the
        E (Exact), S (Substitute) and I (Irrelevant) relevance labels;
        C (Complement) rows were dropped. A reproducible sample (fixed random
        seed 42) of 10,000 queries / 59,270 products / 62,689 judgements was
        selected with a controlled per-query label composition. The file
        data/sample_dataset_ptbr.sample.jsonl is a further 500-query slice of
        that subset.

     b) Machine translation. The natural-language text (product title,
        description, bullet points and colour, and the query strings) was
        translated from English to Brazilian Portuguese (pt-BR) using Amazon
        Translate, with a custom terminology of 26,503 catalog brand terms
        mapped to themselves so that brand names are carried through
        untranslated.

     c) Re-splitting. The original dataset split was replaced with a fresh
        query-level 70/20/10 train/test/validation split (seed 42).

     d) Field reshaping. Records were joined and reshaped into JSONL, and the
        translated product fields were concatenated into a single passage
        field. Query IDs, product IDs and the original ESCI relevance labels
        are PRESERVED UNCHANGED from the source dataset.

   CAVEAT: the Portuguese text is machine-generated and has not been reviewed
   by a human translator. It may contain translation errors. Query-side tokens
   that are not actual catalog brands, or that differ in letter case, were
   translated on a best-effort basis. This data is suitable for demonstrating a
   workflow; it is not a gold-standard human translation and should not be
   presented as one.

